---
description: UI design rules (v0-style consistency)
alwaysApply: true
---

All UI must follow a consistent, minimal SaaS-style design using:

- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui components from `components/ui/*`
- lucide-react icons

Do not introduce any other UI frameworks or styling systems.

Forbidden:
- custom CSS files
- styled-components
- MUI / Chakra / Ant Design / Bootstrap
- inline style objects

---

# Layout Principles

Use simple, predictable layouts.

Default page structure:

Page
 ├ Page Header (title + actions)
 └ Content
    └ Card
       └ Feature content

Rules:
- Avoid complex nested layouts
- Prefer Card containers for grouped content
- Maintain generous spacing and visual hierarchy

Spacing guidelines:
- gap-4 / gap-6 / gap-8
- p-4 / p-6
- space-y-4 / space-y-6

Prefer readability over dense layouts.

---

# Standard UI Patterns

Use consistent UI interaction patterns.

Create / Edit
→ use `Sheet`

Delete / Destructive action
→ use `Dialog` confirmation

Row actions
→ use `DropdownMenu`

Filters
→ place in a horizontal toolbar above lists

Detail view
→ use a `Sheet` or right-side panel

Avoid creating new interaction paradigms.

---

# Component Composition

Prefer composing from shadcn primitives:

Card  
Button  
Input  
Select  
Tabs  
Table  
Badge  
Dialog  
Sheet  
DropdownMenu

Avoid custom-built primitives unless absolutely necessary.

Reuse existing components in `/components` whenever possible.

---

# List Pages

Standard list layout:

Header (title + actions)
Toolbar (filters / search)
Card
 └ Table or list

Lists must include:
- loading state
- empty state
- clear primary action if empty

---

# Forms

Forms must:

- use shadcn input primitives
- maintain consistent spacing
- group fields logically
- avoid overly long vertical forms

Prefer Sheet for editing existing entities.

---

# Responsiveness

Design mobile-first.

Rules:
- layouts must not break on smaller screens
- tables may collapse into stacked views
- avoid fixed widths where possible

---

# Accessibility

Minimum accessibility requirements:

- buttons and inputs must have labels
- dialogs must have titles
- use semantic HTML elements

